WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.600
The prophet Micah looks ahead to
a time of peace among the nations.

2
00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:08.780
Then comes a striking line:
let all the peoples walk,

3
00:00:08.830 --> 00:00:11.280
each one in the name of its god.

4
00:00:11.330 --> 00:00:16.960
But we, the verse goes on, will walk in
the name of the Lord our God for ever.

5
00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:20.610
Yet Judaism does not set out to
make converts of its neighbours,

6
00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:21.940
of any faith.

7
00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:25.280
So if Judaism doesn't
ask the world to convert,

8
00:00:25.330 --> 00:00:27.860
what does it think about other faiths?

9
00:00:27.910 --> 00:00:31.720
In this mission, you'll sort three
attitudes to other religions:

10
00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:35.430
exclusivism, inclusivism and pluralism.

11
00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:40.220
Then you'll see how far Jewish movements
go in dialogue with other faiths.

12
00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:45.170
Your mission: find out what Judaism
teaches about people of other faiths.
